    {
      "title": "OTel Export — Failed Attempts (rate)",
      "description": "yabanin_otel_export_errors_total: failed Export attempts (network errors or non-200 responses from the OTLP collector). This is the OUTAGE signal: exporter failure is visible here without ever affecting consumer latency. A positive rate while drops stay flat means the failure is being absorbed by the bounded queue; sustained failure eventually saturates it — pair this panel with the drop panels above. See docs/observability/otel-export.md.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "PBFA97CFB590B2093" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 16 },
